It allows you to drive:

- light motorcycles (motocicli leggeri), with engine capacity not exceeding 125 cm3, power not exceeding 11 kW and a power/weight ratio not exceeding 0.1 kW/kg;

- motor tricycles with power not exceeding 15 kW;

- quadricycles for the transport of people with an unladen mass of up to 400 kg (for the transport of goods with an unladen mass of up to 550 kg) and power of up to 15 kW;

- agricultural machines that do not exceed the mass and size limits of 'motoveicoli', with a maximum speed of 40 km/h, provided that they do not carry other people besides the driver.

To obtain the A1 licence you must be 16 years old.

The category A1 licence also entitles you to drive the vehicles that can be driven with the AM licence.

It allows the carrying of a passenger only if the driver has reached sixteen years of age and if this possibility is indicated on the vehicle's registration certificate (carta di circolazione).
